# es_MX: fold strong-vowel accents but preserve ñ, ü, í, and ú.
#
# Acute weak vowels distinguish vowel hiatus from glides (hacia/hacía and
# continuo/continúo), so í and ú remain distinct graphemes. Strong-vowel acute
# marks are folded because this segmental model does not encode lexical stress.
# ñ and ü remain phonemic. NFC first makes decomposed inputs follow the same
# protection path before NFD mark removal and restoration.
#
# The bare `:: Null ;` between the restoration rules and the next filter
# directive is intentional: ICU compound rule chains need a no-op
# transliterator there to flush the conversion rules so that the trailing
# `:: Any-Lower ;` actually runs.

:: NFC ;

\u00F1 > \uE001 ;
\u00D1 > \uE002 ;
\u00FC > \uE003 ;
\u00DC > \uE004 ;
\u00ED > \uE005 ;
\u00CD > \uE006 ;
\u00FA > \uE007 ;
\u00DA > \uE008 ;

:: NFD ;
:: [:M:] Remove ;
:: NFC ;

\uE001 > \u00F1 ;
\uE002 > \u00D1 ;
\uE003 > \u00FC ;
\uE004 > \u00DC ;
\uE005 > \u00ED ;
\uE006 > \u00CD ;
\uE007 > \u00FA ;
\uE008 > \u00DA ;

:: Null ;
:: [^-.'[:L:]] Remove ;
:: Any-Lower ;
